Description: This package implements a nuclear family-based algorithm to detect 
    homologous recombination. Using genotypes in PLINK binary format, 
    recombination events are inferred from changes in the inheritance state of 
    informative SNPs between siblings. Closely spaced crossovers that are 
    unlikely to represent true recombination can be filtered out using genetic 
    maps or a SNP-count filter. Additional functions are supplied to detect 
    runs of homozygosity and to phase haplotypes at informative SNPs and 
    intervals that are inferred identical-by-descent. Recombination intervals 
    and runs of homozygosity are returned as `GRanges` objects, and phased 
    genotypes are returned as a `VariantAnnotation` `VCF` object, for use with 
    other Bioconductor packages and genome browsers.
